## Model card

- **Name:** Codestral (Codestral-22B-v0.1)
- **Short description:** Mistral AI’s original open-weight 22B code model (May 2024) designed for low-latency code completion, fill-in-the-middle (FIM), and developer tool assistance across many programming languages.
- **Provider / access:** Mistral AI and open-weight distribution (e.g. Hugging Face `mistralai/Codestral-22B-v0.1`, subject to Mistral’s license terms for that release). Local metadata lists `opencode/codestral`, `noFreeId`.
- **Release / knowledge:** Announced May 29, 2024 (Mistral news). Knowledge cutoff not explicitly stated in reviewed sources.
- **IDs:** `codestral`, `Codestral-22B-v0.1`, `mistralai/Codestral-22B-v0.1`.
- **Context window:** 32,768 tokens native context (later Codestral checkpoints/products extended context in some forms; this report targets the original Codestral/22B-v0.1 identity as represented in this folder).
- **Modalities:** Text and code input/output.
- **Pricing (as of 2026-11-14):** Open-weight availability varies by license/distribution; hosted pricing historically aligned with Codestral-family API offerings in some contexts (local metadata notes $0.30/$0.90 per 1M in/out, $0.03 cached input), but stable current pricing for this exact original checkpoint was not independently confirmed in this pass.
- **Architecture:** Dense transformer code model, ~22B parameters (open-weight). Detailed architecture specifics beyond size not fully disclosed in reviewed sources.

### Raw benchmarks found

> SECOND-PASS SELF-EXCLUSION (updated): Deep second-pass research using alternative web access (`webfetch`, PowerShell `Invoke-WebRequest`) reviewed Mistral’s Codestral announcement, the Hugging Face model card for `mistralai/Codestral-22B-v0.1`, Mistral docs, and local metadata/prior report. Mistral reports code-oriented evaluation results (e.g. HumanEval/MBPP/RepoBench/CruxEval/Spider/multi-language HumanEval/FIM comparisons) primarily via charts/tables in the announcement; in this pass, those results were not clearly extractable as plain-text, independently verifiable standardized numerics for this exact model identity in a form that maps cleanly to this repository’s required scoring categories (SWE-bench, Terminal-Bench, GPQA, AIME, LiveCodeBench, AA indices, etc.). To avoid unverifiable or misattributed scoring, this file remains `.md.excluded` (notes only; scores ignored).

Agent / tool use:

- Designed for completion/FIM and developer assistance rather than autonomous multi-turn agent/tool-loop workflows. Terminal-Bench 2.1 / Tau2 / Tau3 / GDPval-AA / Toolathon / MCP-Atlas: **no verified public score found**.

Reasoning / knowledge:

- GPQA Diamond / HLE / AIME / AA Intelligence Index / LCR / CritPt: **no verified public score found**.

Coding:

- Mistral announcement/HF card describe strong code and FIM performance (including comparisons on HumanEval, MBPP, RepoBench, CruxEval, Spider and multilingual code tasks), but exact standardized numerics were not clearly extractable/verifiable as plain text in this pass for required categories.
- SWE-bench Verified / SWE-Pro / LiveCodeBench / SciCode / Vibe Code Bench: **no verified public score found**.

Long context:

- 32K native context (with later Codestral variants/checkpoints extending context in some products). No standalone long-context retrieval benchmark numeric extracted.

Multimodal:

- Text/code only.

### Source comparison / conflicts

- **Identity/versioning:** “Codestral” can refer to the original 22B open-weight model (`Codestral-22B-v0.1`) and later hosted/updated Codestral variants; this folder targets the original Codestral identity as per local metadata/name. Evidence must be attributed carefully to avoid mixing versions.
- **Benchmarks:** Announcement and model materials emphasize code/FIM strengths but present many results in charts/tables not cleanly extractable in this pass; no directly usable standardized numerics found for required methodology categories.
- **Catalog coverage:** OpenRouter/AA/model-detail pages for the original `codestral` slug were not available as stable benchmarked records in this pass.

